{"title":"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2024 AMC 10A #7</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">2024 AMC 12A #6</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Apex_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Apex Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Don&#39;t_be_tricked!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Don't be tricked!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math_from_my_desk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math from my desk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀_2_min_solve_🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀 2 min solve 🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_MaffyTaffy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by MaffyTaffy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product of three integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the least possible positive sum of the \nthree integers? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585c316a86e0ea3aa32e21c7c1028dcfca43b87c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }2\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }5\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }6\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"364\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We notice that the optimal solution involves two negative numbers and a positive number. Thus we may split <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> into three factors and choose negativity. We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627f84067e15dc34b0bce7b2f77910bd9de8f44e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\cdot6\\cdot1=10\\cdot(-6)\\cdot(-1)=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"250\" height=\"20\" />, and trying other combinations does not yield lesser results so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa56fc57911dcb481c6d97232aa1c47abfaf69e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-6-1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"162\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b6e3b37310da3fdf5a5f57eaa1b0eed7b8f3f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be positive, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be negative. Then we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/922da242415ac45aeabffac11c127df6bda36504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; |b + c|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eac964e50ab7e4904f600a0a12e157a994617fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a18612814be25bcb8a051468222cf90fc6195f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|b + c|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so this doesn't work. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6cc5bbcaca2ea70d1998da025c3f0873bb8562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a344afb74bced3c2f5b1da754ee46022ebcc1eb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,c) = (-6,-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> works, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7afaab7d06f6dc684cec9a9f56b802ae82bcd92c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - 7 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"131\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Pog\" title=\"User:Pog\">pog</a>,~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Mathkiddus\" title=\"User:Mathkiddus\">mathkiddus</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that the most optimal solution would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> negative ones (as seen in solution 1). Let the three integers be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be positive and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be negative. If we want the optimal solution, we want the negative numbers to be as large as possible. so the answer should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a26d1a24bb05fabd68d032b2ba0ef87f00ab3e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-60 \\cdot -1 \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d019d097abc8104036ebc2a81e0b1f97e01b4810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-60 - 1 + 1 = -60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"15\" />... right?\n</p><p>No! Our sum must be positive, so that would be invalid! We see that -<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31e23da74da517c74fd5b0bfb1357206b7e661c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30, -20, -15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d7701e9469f26e22c106341791344b28f3196443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> are too less to allow the sum to be positive. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/3739a912a8cd95513326dd0ff97f03574f14f13f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-15 = z. -15xy=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/6931c38b133392f48a2335047f0cd84596b58b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> to be the most positive, we will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. Yet, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea7a94ed3e3db9e66fee999e15b1d75dc854f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-15+4-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> is still negative. After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d7701e9469f26e22c106341791344b28f3196443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" />, the next factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/3683f227b0b53e6a30087db2fa3b752965ecf05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/3683f227b0b53e6a30087db2fa3b752965ecf05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/0836a0b26fff1454455a8ec7ad809e67e1204805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = -10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />. This might be positive! Now, if we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5cd63c36a51c02eb9aa0a8f9a224f9cd4138cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = -6, y = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/49419f22a79969d918916ca376a7d001da82b1c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 10, x + y + z = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"17\" />. It cannot be smaller because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43970aa97091f384854d477a1e1e07356887266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fd395e96b1e4558dd201a3db8f41306bcbab938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> would result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc8ba1464f944e344427a3009f6db3f0e272247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> being negative. Therefore, our answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4faa3b02b5b2deb20b9cae1911c4231bd3342042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Moonwatcher22\n</p><p>Tiny minor edits made by SuperVince1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Apex_Academy\">Video Solution by Apex Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Apex Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/bXyUErRWq5Q\">https://youtu.be/bXyUErR